FT                   /note="Domain:cl17225:DAHP_synth_1 DAHP synthetase I
FT                   family. NeuB is the prokaryotic N-acetylneuraminic acid
FT                   (Neu5Ac) synthase. It catalyzes the direct formation of
FT                   Neu5Ac (the most common sialic acid) by condensation of
FT                   phosphoenolpyruvate (PEP) and N-acetylmannosamine (ManNAc).
FT                   This reaction has only been observed in prokaryotes;
FT                   eukaryotes synthesize the 9-phosphate form, Neu5Ac-9-P, and
FT                   utilize ManNAc-6-P instead of ManNAc. Such eukaryotic
FT                   enzymes are not present in this family. This family also
FT                   contains SpsE spore coat polysaccharide biosynthesis
FT                   proteins. [Superfamily, Aligned:13-344, Eval:4.9e-173,
FT                   score:482.1]"
