FT                   Eval:2.7e-168]"
FT                   /note="Domain:cl26360:PcaH Protocatechuate 3,4-dioxygenase
FT                   beta subunit  [Secondary metabolites biosynthesis,
FT                   transport and catabolism]. Members of this family known so
FT                   far are catechol 1,2-dioxygenases of the Proteobacteria.
FT                   They are distinct from catechol 1,2-dioxygenases and
FT                   chlorocatechol 1,2-dioxygenases of the Actinobacteria,
FT                   which are quite similar to each other and resolved by
FT                   separate models. This enzyme catalyzes intradiol cleavage
FT                   in which catechol + O2 becomes cis,cis-muconate. Catechol
FT                   is an intermediate in the catabolism of many different
FT                   aromatic compounds, as is the alternative intermediate
FT                   protocatechuate. In Acinetobacter lwoffii, two isozymes are
FT                   present with abilities, differing somewhat, to act on
FT                   catechol analogs 3-methylcatechol, 4-methylcatechol,
FT                   4-methoxycatechol, and 4-chlorocatechol. [Energy
FT                   metabolism, Other] [Superfamily, Aligned:92-276,
FT                   Eval:1.8e-32, score:117.1]"
