FT                   proteins. PilW is one of the component proteins of the
FT                   pilus biogenesis process whereby pilus fibres are assembled
FT                   in the periplasm, emerge onto the cell surface and are
FT                   there stabilized, to allow bacterial attachment to host
FT                   cells. PilW is an outer-membrane protein necessary for both
FT                   the functionality of fibres and their stabilisation.
