FT                   /note="Domain:cl00208:RNase_T2 N/A. Ribonuclease T2 (RNase
FT                   T2) is a widespread family of secreted RNases found in
FT                   every organism examined thus far.  This family includes
FT                   RNase Rh, RNase MC1, RNase LE, and self-incompatibility
FT                   RNases (S-RNases).  Plant T2 RNases are expressed during
FT                   leaf senescence in order to scavenge phosphate from
FT                   ribonucleotides. They are also expressed in response to
FT                   wounding or pathogen invasion. S-RNases are thought to
FT                   prevent self-fertilization by acting as selective
FT                   cytotoxins of 'self' pollen. Generally, RNases have two
FT                   distinct binding sites: the primary site (B1 site) and the
FT                   subsite (B2 site), for nucleotides located at the 5'- and
FT                   3'- terminal ends of the sessil bond, respectively. This CD
FT                   includes the prokaryotic RNase T2 family members.
FT                   [Superfamily, Aligned:7-175, Eval:1.6e-13, score:63.6,
FT                   N-term missing]"
FT                   /note="MGA_546"
