FT                   /note="Domain:cl27682:SBP_bac_3 Bacterial extracellular
FT                   solute-binding proteins, family 3. This subfamily belongs
FT                   to bacterial extracellular solute-binding protein family 3
FT                   (pfam00497). In that family, most members are ABC
FT                   transporter periplasmic substrate-binding proteins.
FT                   However, members of the present subfamily are orphans in
FT                   the sense of being adjacent to neither ABC transporter
FT                   ATP-binding proteins or permease subunits. Instead, most
FT                   members are encoded next to the two signature proteins of
FT                   the proposed Glycine-Rich Repeat Modification (GRRM)
FT                   system, a radical SAM/SPASM protein GrrM (TIGR04261) and
FT                   the Gly-rich repeat protein itself GrrA (TIGR04260).
