FT                   /note="Domain:cl09208:Tim44 Tim44-like domain. Mba1 is an
FT                   inner membrane protein that is part of the mitochondrial
FT                   protein export machinery. It binds to the large subunit of
FT                   mitochondrial ribosomes and cooperates with the C-terminal
FT                   ribosome-binding domain of Oxa1, which is a central
FT                   component of the insertion machinery of the inner membrane.
FT                   In the absence of both Mba1 and the C-terminus of Oxa1,
FT                   mitochondrial translation products fail to be properly
FT                   inserted into the inner membrane and serve as substrates of
FT                   the matrix chaperone Hsp70. It is proposed that Mba1
FT                   functions as a ribosome receptor that cooperates with Oxa1
FT                   in the positioning of the ribosome exit site to the
FT                   insertion machinery of the inner membrane. [Superfamily,
FT                   Aligned:127-325, Eval:1.7e-12, score:63.6, N-term missing]"
