FT                   /note="Domain:cl25545:V-ATPase_G_2 Vacuolar (H+)-ATPase G
FT                   subunit. TolA couples the inner membrane complex of itself
FT                   with TolQ and TolR to the outer membrane complex of TolB
FT                   and OprL (also called Pal). Most of the length of the
FT                   protein consists of low-complexity sequence that may differ
FT                   in both length and composition from one species to another,
FT                   complicating efforts to discriminate TolA (the most
FT                   divergent gene in the tol-pal system) from paralogs such as
FT                   TonB. Selection of members of the seed alignment and
FT                   criteria for setting scoring cutoffs are based largely
FT                   conserved operon struction. //The Tol-Pal complex is
FT                   required for maintaining outer membrane integrity. Also
FT                   involved in transport (uptake) of colicins and filamentous
FT                   DNA, and implicated in pathogenesis. Transport is energized
FT                   by the proton motive force. TolA is an inner membrane
FT                   protein that interacts with periplasmic TolB and with outer
FT                   membrane porins ompC, phoE and lamB. [Transport and binding
FT                   proteins, Other, Cellular processes, Pathogenesis]
FT                   [Superfamily, Aligned:137-446, Eval:1.8e-11, score:62.3]"
