FT                   /note="Domain:cl26231:YdhJ HD superfamily phosphohydrolase
FT                   [General function prediction only]. dGTP
FT                   triphosphohydrolase (dgt) releases inorganic triphosphate,
FT                   an unusual activity reaction product, from GTP. Its
FT                   activity has been called limited to the Enterobacteriaceae,
FT                   although homologous sequences are detected elsewhere. This
FT                   finding casts doubt on whether the activity is shared in
FT                   other species. In several of these other species, the
FT                   homologous gene is found in an apparent operon with dnaG,
FT                   the DNA primase gene. The enzyme from E. coli was shown to
FT                   bind coopertatively to single stranded DNA. The biological
FT                   role of dgt is unknown. [Purines, pyrimidines, nucleosides,
FT                   and nucleotides, Nucleotide and nucleoside
FT                   interconversions] [Superfamily, Aligned:4-440,
