FT                   Eval:1.0e-114]"
FT                   /note="Domain:cl21460:HAD_like Haloacid Dehalogenase-like
FT                   Hydrolases. This subfamily includes the uncharacterized
FT                   Bacillus subtilis YhcW. It belongs to the
FT                   beta-phosphoglucomutase-like family whose other members
FT                   include Lactococcus lactis beta-PGM, a mutase which
FT                   catalyzes the interconversion of beta-D-glucose 1-phosphate
FT                   (G1P) and D-glucose 6-phosphate (G6P), Saccharomyces
FT                   cerevisiae phosphatases GPP1 and GPP2 that dephosphorylate
FT                   DL-glycerol-3-phosphate and DOG1 and DOG2 that
FT                   dephosphorylate 2-deoxyglucose-6-phosphate, and Escherichia
FT                   coli 6-phosphogluconate phosphatase YieH. This family
FT                   belongs to the haloacid dehalogenase-like (HAD) hydrolases,
FT                   a large superfamily of diverse enzymes that catalyze carbon
FT                   or phosphoryl group transfer reactions on a range of
FT                   substrates, using an active site aspartate in nucleophilic
FT                   catalysis. Members of this superfamily include
FT                   2-L-haloalkanoic acid dehalogenase, azetidine hydrolase,
FT                   phosphonoacetaldehyde hydrolase, phosphoserine phosphatase,
FT                   phosphomannomutase, P-type ATPases and many others. HAD
FT                   hydrolases are found in all three kingdoms of life, and
FT                   most genomes are predicted to contain multiple HAD-like
FT                   proteins. Members possess a highly conserved alpha/beta
FT                   core domain, and many also possess a small cap domain, the
FT                   fold and function of which is variable. HAD hydrolases are
FT                   sometimes referred to as belonging to the DDDD superfamily
FT                   of phosphohydrolases. [Superfamily, Aligned:12-208,
FT                   Eval:7.6e-24, score:91.6]"
FT                   /note="MGA_714"
