FT                   /note="Domain:cl25563:Mal_decarbox_Al Malonate
FT                   decarboxylase, alpha subunit, transporter. This model
FT                   describes malonate decarboxylase alpha subunit, from both
FT                   the water-soluble form as found in Klebsiella pneumoniae
FT                   and the form couple to sodium ion pumping in Malonomonas
FT                   rubra. Malonate decarboxylase Na+ pump is the paradigm of
FT                   the family of Na+ transport decarboxylases. Essentially, it
FT                   couples the energy derived from decarboxylation of a
FT                   carboxylic acid substrate to move Na+ ion across the
FT                   bilayer. Functional malonate decarboylase is a multi
FT                   subunit protein. The alpha subunit enzymatically performs
FT                   the transfer of malonate (substrate) to an acyl carrier
FT                   protein subunit for subsequent decarboxylation, hence the
FT                   name: acetyl-S-acyl carrier protein:malonate carrier
FT                   protein-SH transferase. [Transport and binding proteins,
FT                   Cations and iron carrying compounds, Energy metabolism,
FT                   Other] [Superfamily, Aligned:148-220, Eval:8.2e-07,
FT                   score:48.5, C-term missing]"
