FT                   /note="Domain:cl00596:LrgB LrgB-like family. Members of
FT                   this small but broadly distibuted (Gram-positive,
FT                   Gram-negative, and Archaeal) family appear to have multiple
FT                   transmembrane segments. The function is unknown. A homolog,
FT                   LrgB of Staphylococcus aureus, in the same small
FT                   superfamily but in an outgroup to this subfamily, is
FT                   regulated by LytSR and is suggested to act as a murein
FT                   hydrolase. Of the three paralogous proteins in B. subtilis,
FT                   one is a full length member of this family, one lacks the
FT                   C-terminal 60 residues and has an additional 128 N-terminal
FT                   residues but branches within the family in a phylogenetic
FT                   tree, and one is closely related to LrgB and part of the
FT                   outgroup. [Hypothetical proteins, Conserved] [Superfamily,
FT                   Aligned:5-225, Eval:3.5e-63, score:193.9]"
