FT                   /note="Domain:cl26210:MFS_2 MFS/sugar transport protein.
FT                   The Glycoside-Pentoside-Hexuronide (GPH):Cation Symporter
FT                   Family (TC 2.A.2) GPH:cation symporters catalyze uptake of
FT                   sugars in symport with a monovalent cation (H+ or Na+).
FT                   Members of this family includes transporters for melibiose,
FT                   lactose, raffinose, glucuronides, pentosides and
FT                   isoprimeverose. Mutants of two groups of these symporters
FT                   (the melibiose permeases of enteric bacteria, and the
FT                   lactose permease of Streptococcus thermophilus) have been
FT                   isolated in which altered cation specificity is observed or
FT                   in which sugar transport is uncoupled from cation symport
FT                   (i.e., uniport is catalyzed). The various members of the
FT                   family can use Na+, H+ or Li, Na+ or Li+, H+ or Li+, or
FT                   only H+ as the symported cation. All of these proteins
FT                   possess twelve putative transmembrane a-helical spanners.
FT                   [Transport and binding proteins, Carbohydrates, organic
FT                   alcohols, and acids] [Superfamily, Aligned:149-385,
FT                   Eval:1.9e-07, score:49.9, N-term missing]"
