FT                   /note="Domain:cl15774:Hemerythrin-like Hemerythrin family.
FT                   Iteration of the HHE family found it to be related to
FT                   Hemerythrin. It also demonstrated that what has been
FT                   described as a single domain in fact consists of two cation
FT                   binding domains. Members of this family occur all across
FT                   nature and are involved in a variety of processes. For
FT                   instance, in Nereis diversicolor hemerythrin binds Cadmium
FT                   so as to protect the organism from toxicity. However
FT                   Hemerythrin is classically described as Oxygen-binding
FT                   through two attached Fe2+ ions. And the bacterial NorA is a
FT                   regulator of response to NO, which suggests yet another
FT                   set-up for its metal ligands. In Staphylococcus aureus the
FT                   iron-sulfur cluster repair protein ScdA has been noted to
FT                   be important when the organism switches to living in
FT                   environments with low oxygen concentrations; perhaps this
FT                   protein acts as an oxygen store or scavenger. [Superfamily,
FT                   Aligned:1-137, Eval:7.0e-21, score:80.1]"
FT                   /note="MGA_1027"
