FT                   /note="Domain:cl28567:HI1514 Phage tail tape-measure
FT                   protein, controls tail length   [Mobilome: prophages,
FT                   transposons]. Proteins containing this domain are strictly
FT                   bacterial, including bacteriophage and prophage regions of
FT                   bacterial genomes. Most members are 800 to 1800 amino acids
FT                   long, making them among the longest predicted proteins of
FT                   their respective phage genomes, where they are encoded in
FT                   tail protein regions. This roughly 80-residue domain
FT                   described here usually begins between residue 100 and 250.
FT                   Many members are known or predicted to act as phage tail
FT                   tape measure proteins, a minor tail component that
FT                   regulates tail length. [Superfamily, Aligned:314-404,
FT                   Eval:5.0e-08, score:53.3, N-term missing]"
