FT                   /note="Domain:cl26861:CirA Outer membrane receptor
FT                   proteins, mostly Fe transport [Inorganic ion transport and
FT                   metabolism]. This model represents a family of
FT                   TonB-dependent outer membrane receptor/transporters acting
FT                   on iron-containing proteins such as hemoglobin, transferrin
FT                   and lactoferrin. Two subfamily models with a narrower scope
FT                   are contained within this model, the heme/hemoglobin
FT                   receptor family protein model (TIGR01785) and the
FT                   transferrin/lactoferrin receptor family model (TIGR01776).
FT                   Accessions which score above trusted to this model while
FT                   not scoring above trusted to the more specific models are
FT                   most likely to be hemoglobin transporters. Nearly all of
FT                   the species containing trusted hits to this model have
FT                   access to hemoglobin, transferrin or lactoferrin or related
FT                   proteins in their biological niche. [Transport and binding
FT                   proteins, Cations and iron carrying compounds, Transport
