FT                   /note="Domain:cl27264:CorC_HlyC Transporter associated
FT                   domain. Members of this protein family are exclusive to the
FT                   Bacteroidetes phylum (previously
FT                   Cytophaga-Flavobacteria-Bacteroides). GldC is a protein
FT                   linked to a type of rapid surface gliding motility found in
FT                   certain Bacteroidetes, such as Flavobacterium johnsoniae
FT                   and Cytophaga hutchinsonii. GldE was discovered because of
FT                   its adjacency to GldD in F. johnsonii. Overexpression of
FT                   GldE partially supresses the effects of a GldB point mutant
FT                   suggesting that GldB and GldE interact. Gliding motility
FT                   appears closely linked to chitin utilization in the model
FT                   species Flavobacterium johnsoniae. Not all Bacteroidetes
FT                   with members of this protein family appear to have all of
FT                   the genes associated with gliding motility and in fact some
FT                   do not appear to express the gliding phenotype.
FT                   [Superfamily, Aligned:22-276, Eval:3.1e-87, score:259.2]"
FT                   /note="MGA_1338"
