FT                   /note="Domain:cl11971:PPK2 Polyphosphate kinase 2 (PPK2).
FT                   Members of this protein family belong to the polyphosphate
FT                   kinase 2 (PPK2) family, which is not related in sequence to
FT                   PPK1. While PPK1 tends to act in the biosynthesis of
FT                   polyphosphate, or poly(P), members of the PPK2 family tend
FT                   to use the terminal phosphate of poly(P) to regenerate ATP
FT                   or GTP from the corresponding nucleoside diphosphate, or
FT                   ADP from AMP as is the case with polyphosphate:AMP
FT                   phosphotransferase (PAP). Members of this protein family
FT                   most likely transfer the terminal phosphate between poly(P)
FT                   and some nucleotide, but it is not clear which. [Central
FT                   intermediary metabolism, Phosphorus compounds]
FT                   [Superfamily, Aligned:247-469, Eval:5.4e-86, score:262.3]"
