FT                   /note="Domain:cl27617:UDPG_MGDP_dh UDP-glucose/GDP-mannose
FT                   dehydrogenase family, central domain. Enzymes in this
FT                   family catalyze the NAD-dependent alcohol-to-acid oxidation
FT                   of nucleotide-linked sugars. Examples include UDP-glucose
FT                   6-dehydrogenase (1.1.1.22), GDP-mannose 6-dehydrogenase
FT                   (1.1.1.132), UDP-N-acetylglucosamine 6-dehydrogenase
FT                   (1.1.1.136), UDP-N-acetyl-D-galactosaminuronic acid
FT                   dehydrogenase, and UDP-N-acetyl-D-mannosaminuronic acid
FT                   dehydrogenase. These enzymes are most often involved in the
FT                   biosynthesis of polysaccharides and are often found in
FT                   operons devoted to that purpose. All of these enzymes
FT                   contain three Pfam domains, pfam03721, pfam00984, and
FT                   pfam03720 for the N-terminal, central, and C-terminal
FT                   regions respectively. [Superfamily, Aligned:6-419,
FT                   Eval:2.6e-175, score:494.5]"
