FT                   /note="Domain:cl26457:T2SSJ Type II secretion system
FT                   (T2SS), protein J. This model represents GspJ, one of two
FT                   proteins highly conserved at their N-termini and described
FT                   by pfam02501 but easily separable phylogenetically. The
FT                   other is GspI. Both GspI and GspJ are proteins of the type
FT                   II secretion pathway, or main terminal branch of the
FT                   general secretion pathway. This pathway carries proteins
FT                   across the outer membrane. Note that proteins of type II
FT                   secretion are cryptic in E. coli K-12 - present but not yet
FT                   demonstrated to act on any target. [Superfamily,
FT                   Aligned:3-121, Eval:1.1e-08, score:50.1, C-term missing]"
