FT                   [Category:O, Aligned:160-258, Eval:2.3e-07, score:47.1,
FT                   C-term missing]"
FT                   /note="Domain:cl25457:GrxB Glutaredoxin 2
FT                   [Posttranslational modification, protein turnover,
FT                   chaperones]. Glutaredoxins are thioltransferases (disulfide
FT                   reductases) which utilize glutathione and NADPH as
FT                   cofactors. Oxidized glutathione is regenerated by
FT                   glutathione reductase. Together these components compose
FT                   the glutathione system. Glutaredoxins utilize the CXXC
FT                   motif common to thioredoxins and are involved in multiple
FT                   cellular processes including protection from redox stress,
FT                   reduction of critical enzymes such as ribonucleotide
FT                   reductase and the generation of reduced sulfur for iron
FT                   sulfur cluster formation. Glutaredoxins are capable of
FT                   reduction of mixed disulfides of glutathione as well as the
FT                   formation of glutathione mixed disulfides. This model
FT                   includes the highly abundant E. coli GrxB (Grx2)
FT                   glutaredoxin which is notably longer than either GrxA or
FT                   GrxC. Unlike the other two E. coli glutaredoxins, GrxB
FT                   appears to be unable to reduce ribonucleotide reductase,
FT                   and may have more to do with resistance to redox stress.
FT                   [Energy metabolism, Electron transport] [Superfamily,
FT                   Aligned:36-118, Eval:4.2e-07, score:46.3, C-term missing]"
FT                   /note="MGA_1692"
