FT                   /note="Domain:cl25633:HlyD HlyD membrane-fusion protein of
FT                   T1SS. HlyD_D23 is the combined domains 2 and 3 of the
FT                   membrane-fusion proteins CusB and HlyD, which forms a
FT                   barrel-sandwich. CusB and HlyD proteins are membrane fusion
FT                   proteins of the CusCFBA copper efflux system in E.coli and
FT                   related bacteria. The whole molecule hinges between D2 and
FT                   D3. Efflux systems of this resistance-nodulation-division
FT                   group - RND - have been developed to excrete poisonous
FT                   metal ions, and in E.coli the only one that deals with
FT                   silver and copper is the CusA transporter. The transporter
FT                   CusA works in conjunction with a periplasmic component that
FT                   is a membrane fusion protein, eg CusB, and an
FT                   outer-membrane channel component CusC in a CusABC complex
FT                   driven by import of protons. [Superfamily, Aligned:4-274,
FT                   Eval:5.2e-27, score:106.3, C-term missing]"
