FT                   /note="Domain:cl01226:T6SS_HCP Type VI secretion system
FT                   effector, Hcp. This family includes Hcp1 (hemolysin
FT                   coregulated protein 1), an exported, homohexameric
FT                   ring-forming virulence protein from Pseudomonas aeruginosa.
FT                   Hcp1 lacks a conventional signal sequence and is instead
FT                   exported by means of the type VI secretion system, encoded
FT                   by a pathogenicity cluster of a class previously designated
FT                   IAHP (IcmF-associated homologous protein). Homologs of
FT                   Hcp1, in this protein family, are found in various bacteria
FT                   of which most but not all are known pathogens. Pathogens
FT                   may have many multiple members of this family, with three
FT                   to ten in Erwinia carotovora, Yersinia pestis,
FT                   uropathogenic Escherichia coli, and the insect pathogen
FT                   Photorhabdus luminescens. [Cellular processes,
FT                   Pathogenesis] [Superfamily, Aligned:1-148, Eval:1.2e-41,
