FT                   /note="Domain:cl27361:Biotin_carb_C Biotin carboxylase
FT                   C-terminal domain. Members of this family are ATP-dependent
FT                   urea carboxylase, including characterized members from
FT                   Oleomonas sagaranensis (alpha class Proteobacterium) and
FT                   yeasts such as Saccharomyces cerevisiae. The allophanate
FT                   hydrolase domain of the yeast enzyme is not included in
FT                   this model and is represented by an adjacent gene in
FT                   Oleomonas sagaranensis. The fusion of urea carboxylase and
FT                   allophanate hydrolase is designated urea amidolyase. The
FT                   enzyme from Oleomonas sagaranensis was shown to be highly
FT                   active on acetamide and formamide as well as urea. [Central
FT                   intermediary metabolism, Nitrogen metabolism] [Superfamily,
