FT                   /note="Domain:cl26994:Glyco_hydro_108 Glycosyl hydrolase
FT                   108. This family acts as a lysozyme (N-acetylmuramidase),
FT                   EC:3.2.1.17. It contains a conserved EGGY motif near the
FT                   N-terminus, the glutamic acid within this motif is
FT                   essential for catalytic activity. In bacteria, it may
FT                   activate the secretion of large proteins via the breaking
FT                   and rearrangement of the peptidoglycan layer during
FT                   secretion. It is frequently found at the N-terminus of
FT                   proteins containing a C-terminal pfam09374 domain.
