FT                   /note="Domain:cl27026:AXE1 Acetyl xylan esterase (AXE1).
FT                   This family consists of several bacterial acetyl xylan
FT                   esterase proteins. Acetyl xylan esterases are enzymes that
FT                   hydrolyse the ester linkages of the acetyl groups in
FT                   position 2 and/or 3 of the xylose moieties of natural
FT                   acetylated xylan from hardwood. These enzymes are one of
FT                   the accessory enzymes which are part of the xylanolytic
FT                   system, together with xylanases, beta-xylosidases,
FT                   alpha-arabinofuranosidases and methylglucuronidases; these
FT                   are all required for the complete hydrolysis of xylan.
