FT                   /note="Domain:cl01171:RelB RelB antitoxin. Plasmids may be
FT                   maintained stably in bacterial populations through the
FT                   action of addiction modules, in which a toxin and antidote
FT                   are encoded in a cassette on the plasmid. In any daughter
FT                   cell that lacks the plasmid, the toxin persists and is
FT                   lethal after the antidote protein is depleted.
FT                   Toxin/antitoxin pairs are also found on main chromosomes,
FT                   and likely represent selfish DNA. Sequences in the seed for
FT                   this alignment all were found adjacent to toxin genes. The
FT                   resulting model appears to describe a narrower set of
FT                   proteins than pfam04221, although many in the scope of this
FT                   model are not obviously paired with toxin proteins. Several
FT                   toxin/antitoxin pairs may occur in a single species.
