FT                   /note="Domain:cl00615:Membrane-FADS-like N/A. Beta-carotene
FT                   hydroxylase (CrtR), the carotenoid zeaxanthin biosynthetic
FT                   enzyme catalyzes the addition of hydroxyl groups to the
FT                   beta-ionone rings of beta-carotene to form zeaxanthin and
FT                   is found in bacteria and red algae. Carotenoids are
FT                   important natural pigments; zeaxanthin and lutein are the
FT                   only dietary carotenoids that accumulate in the macular
FT                   region of the retina and lens. It is proposed that these
FT                   carotenoids protect ocular tissues against photooxidative
FT                   damage. CrtR does not show overall amino acid sequence
FT                   similarity to the beta-carotene hydroxylases similar to
FT                   CrtZ, an astaxanthin biosynthetic beta-carotene
FT                   hydroxylase. However, CrtR does show sequence similarity to
FT                   the green alga, Haematococcus pluvialis, beta-carotene
FT                   ketolase (CrtW), which converts beta-carotene to
FT                   canthaxanthin. Sequences of the
FT                   CrtR_beta-carotene-hydroxylase domain family, as well as,
FT                   the CrtW_beta-carotene-ketolase domain family appear to be
FT                   structurally related to membrane fatty acid desaturases and
FT                   alkane hydroxylases. They all share in common extensive
FT                   hydrophobic regions that would be capable of spanning the
FT                   membrane bilayer at least twice. Comparison of these
FT                   sequences also reveals three regions of conserved histidine
FT                   cluster motifs that contain eight histidine residues:
FT                   HXXXH, HXXHH, and HXXHH. These histidine residues are
FT                   reported to be catalytically essential and proposed to be
FT                   the ligands for the iron atoms contained within homologs,
FT                   stearoyl CoA desaturase and alkane hydroxylase.
FT                   [Superfamily, Aligned:46-285, Eval:2.0e-70, score:220.3]"
FT                   /note="MGA_2333"
