FT                   /note="Domain:cl26250:TPR_6 Tetratricopeptide repeat.
FT                   Members of this protein family are the product of one of
FT                   seven genes regularly clustered in operons to encode the
FT                   proteins of the tol-pal system, which is critical for
FT                   maintaining the integrity of the bacterial outer membrane.
FT                   The gene for this periplasmic protein has been designated
FT                   orf2 and ybgF. All members of the seed alignment were from
FT                   unique tol-pal gene regions from completed bacterial
FT                   genomes. The architecture of this protein is a signal
FT                   sequence, a low-complexity region usually rich in Asn and
FT                   Gln, a well-conserved region with tandem repeats that
FT                   resemble the tetratricopeptide (TPR) repeat, involved in
