FT                   bias:23.9]"
FT                   /note="Domain:cl01087:MreD rod shape-determining protein
FT                   MreD. Members of this protein family are the MreD protein
FT                   of bacterial cell shape determination. Most rod-shaped
FT                   bacteria depend on MreB and RodA to achieve either a rod
FT                   shape or some other non-spherical morphology such as coil
FT                   or stalk formation. MreD is encoded in an operon with MreB,
FT                   and often with RodA and PBP-2 as well. It is highly
FT                   hydrophobic (therefore somewhat low-complexity) and highly
FT                   divergent, and therefore sometimes tricky to discover by
FT                   homology, but this model finds most examples. [Cell
FT                   envelope, Biosynthesis and degradation of murein sacculus
FT                   and peptidoglycan] [Superfamily, Aligned:7-155,
FT                   Eval:5.8e-12, score:57.6]"
