FT                   /note="Domain:cl09153:PhdYeFM_antitox Antitoxin Phd_YefM,
FT                   type II toxin-antitoxin system. This model recognizes a
FT                   region of about 55 amino acids toward the N-terminal end of
FT                   bacterial proteins of about 85 amino acids in length. The
FT                   best-characterized member is prevent-host-death (phd) of
FT                   bacteriophage P1, the antidote partner of death-on-curing
FT                   (doc) (TIGR01550) in an addiction module. Addiction modules
FT                   prevent plasmid curing by killing the host cell as the
FT                   longer-lived killing protein persists while the gene for
FT                   the shorter-lived antidote is lost. Note, however, that
FT                   relatively few members of this family appear to be plasmid
FT                   or phage-encoded. Also, there is little overlap, except for
FT                   phage P1 itself, of species with this family and with the
FT                   doc family. [Cellular processes, Toxin production and
FT                   resistance, Mobile and extrachromosomal element functions,
FT                   Other] [Superfamily, Aligned:1-47, Eval:5.8e-08,
FT                   score:42.4, C-term missing]"
