FT                   /note="Domain:cl27678:AMP-binding AMP-binding enzyme.
FT                   Proteins in this family belong to the AMP-binding enzyme
FT                   family (pfam00501). Members activate 2,3-dihydroxybenzoate
FT                   (DHB) by ligation of AMP from ATP with the release of
FT                   pyrophosphate; many are involved in synthesis of
FT                   siderophores such as enterobactin, vibriobactin,
FT                   vulnibactin, etc. The most closely related proteine
FT                   believed to differ in function activates salicylate rather
FT                   than DHB. [Transport and binding proteins, Cations and iron
FT                   carrying compounds] [Superfamily, Aligned:1-540,
FT                   Eval:0.0e+00, score:813.6]"
