FT                   /note="Domain:cl28369:PncB Nicotinic acid
FT                   phosphoribosyltransferase [Coenzyme transport and
FT                   metabolism]. A deep split separates two related families of
FT                   proteins, one of which includes experimentally
FT                   characterized examples of nicotinate
FT                   phosphoribosyltransferase, an the first enzyme of NAD
FT                   salvage biosynthesis. This model represents the other
FT                   family. Members have a different (longer) spacing of
FT                   several key motifs and have an additional C-terminal domain
FT                   of up to 100 residues. One argument suggesting that this
FT                   family represents the same enzyme is that no species has a
FT                   member of both families. Another is that the gene encoding
FT                   this protein is located near other NAD salvage biosynthesis
FT                   genes in Nostoc and in at least four different
FT                   Gram-positive bacteria. NAD and NADP are ubiquitous in
FT                   life. Most members of this family are Gram-positive
FT                   bacteria. An additional set of mutually closely related
FT                   archaeal sequences score between the trusted and noise
FT                   cutoffs. [Biosynthesis of cofactors, prosthetic groups, and
FT                   carriers, Pyridine nucleotides] [Superfamily,
FT                   Aligned:12-493, Eval:6.2e-34, score:129.3]"
FT                   /note="MGA_2938"
