FT                   /note="Domain:cl00448:SurE Survival protein SurE. This
FT                   protein family originally was named SurE because of its
FT                   role in stationary phase survivalin Escherichia coli. In E.
FT                   coli, surE is next to pcm, an L-isoaspartyl protein repair
FT                   methyltransferase that is also required for stationary
FT                   phase survival. Recent work () shows that viewing SurE as
FT                   an acid phosphatase (3.1.3.2) is not accurate. Rather, SurE
FT                   in E. coli, Thermotoga maritima, and Pyrobaculum aerophilum
FT                   acts strictly on nucleoside 5'- and 3'-monophosphates. E.
FT                   coli SurE is Recommended cutoffs are 15 for homology, 40
FT                   for probable orthology, and 200 for orthology with
FT                   full-length homology. [Cellular processes, Adaptations to
FT                   atypical conditions] [Superfamily, Aligned:21-313,
