FT                   /note="Domain:cl00838:FeoA FeoA domain. This domain also
FT                   occurs at the C-terminus in related proteins. The
FT                   transporter Feo is composed of three proteins: FeoA a
FT                   small, soluble SH3-domain protein probably located in the
FT                   cytosol; FeoB, a large protein with a cytosolic N-terminal
FT                   G-protein domain and a C-terminal integral inner-membrane
FT                   domain containing two 'Gate' motifs which likely functions
FT                   as the Fe2+ permease; and FeoC, a small protein apparently
FT                   functioning as an [Fe-S]-dependent transcriptional
FT                   repressor. Feo allows the bacterial cell to acquire iron
FT                   from its environment. [Superfamily, Aligned:15-95,
FT                   Eval:5.9e-14, score:58.4]"
