FT                   /note="Domain:cl27494:YgfZ Folate-binding Fe-S cluster
FT                   repair protein YgfZ, possible role in tRNA modification
FT                   [Posttranslational modification, protein turnover,
FT                   chaperones]. YgfZ is a protein from Escherichia coli,
FT                   homologous to the glycine cleavage system T protein, or
FT                   aminomethyltransferase, GcvT (TIGR00528). Homologs of YgfZ
FT                   other than members of the GcvT family share a
FT                   well-conserved signature region that includes the motif,
FT                   KGCYxGQE. Elsewhere, sequence diverge and length variation
FT                   are substantial. Members of this family are mostly
FT                   bacterial, largely absent from the Firmicutes and otherwise
FT                   usually present. A few eukaryotic examples are found among
FT                   the Apicomplexa, and a few archaeal sequences are found.
FT                   Two functions implicated for this folate-binding protein
FT                   are RNA modification (a function likely to be conserved)
FT                   and replication initiation (a function likely to be highly
FT                   variable). Many members of this family are, at the time of
FT                   construction of this model, misnamed as the glycine
FT                   cleavage system T protein. [Biosynthesis of cofactors,
FT                   prosthetic groups, and carriers, Other] [Superfamily,
FT                   Aligned:1-233, Eval:2.5e-33, score:119.4]"
