FT                   /note="Domain:cl19845:NAGPA Phosphodiester glycosidase.
FT                   This is a family conserved from bacteria to humans. The
FT                   structure of a member from Bacteroides has been
FT                   crystallized and modelled onto the luminal region of the
FT                   human member of the family, the transmembrane glycoprotein
FT                   N-acetylglucosamine-1-phosphodiester
FT                   alpha-N-acetylglucosaminidase. There is some conservation
FT                   of potentially functional residues, implying that in the
FT                   bacterial members this family acts in some way as a
FT                   phosphodiester glycosidase. The human protein is also
FT                   present, so the eukaryotic members are likely to be
FT                   catalyzing the second step in the formation of the mannose
FT                   6-phosphate targeting signal on lysosomal enzyme
FT                   oligosaccharides. [Superfamily, Aligned:42-242,
FT                   Eval:1.4e-85, score:252.4]"
