FT                   /note="Domain:cl27048:BTP Chlorhexidine efflux transporter.
FT                   This family represents a conserved pair of two
FT                   transmembrane alpha-helices. All members carry the two
FT                   pairs of TMs. BTP is a form of drug efflux pump, that
FT                   actively tranports chlorhexidine out of the cell.
FT                   Chlorhexidine, a bisbiguanide antimicrobial agent, is
FT                   commonly used as an antiseptic and disinfectant in
FT                   hospitals, and there is an increasing problem with
FT                   resistance to it in some pathogenic bacteria. BTP is
FT                   localized in the cytoplasmic membrane. [Superfamily,
