FT                   /note="Domain:cl00296:Peptidase_C39_like N/A. BtrH_N is the
FT                   N-terminus of the acyl carrier protein:aminoglycoside
FT                   acyltransferase BtrH. Alternatively it can be referred to
FT                   as butirosin biosynthesis protein H. BtrH transfers the
FT                   unique (S)-4-amino-2-hydroxybutyrate (AHBA) side chain,
FT                   which protects the antibiotic butirosin from several common
FT                   resistance mechanisms. Butirosin, an aminoglycoside
FT                   antibiotic produced by Bacillus circulans, exhibits
FT                   improved antibiotic properties over its parent molecule and
FT                   retains bactericidal activity toward many
FT                   aminoglycoside-resistant strains. Butirosin is unique in
FT                   carrying the AHBA side-chain. BtrH transfers the AHBA from
FT                   the acyl carrier protein BtrI to the parent aminoglycoside
FT                   ribostamycin as a gamma-glutamylated dipeptide.
