FT                   /note="Domain:cl26706:RsbU Serine phosphatase RsbU,
FT                   regulator of sigma subunit  [Signal transduction
FT                   mechanisms, Transcription]. Stage II sporulation protein E
FT                   (SpoIIE) is a multiple membrane spanning protein with two
FT                   separable functions. It plays a role in the switch to polar
FT                   cell division during sporulation. By means of it protein
FT                   phosphatase activity, located in the C-terminal region, it
FT                   activates sigma-F. All proteins that score above the
FT                   trusted cutoff to this model are found in endospore-forming
FT                   Gram-positive bacteria. Surprisingly, a sequence from the
FT                   Cyanobacterium-like (and presumably non-spore-forming)
FT                   photosynthesizer Heliobacillus mobilis is homologous, and
