FT                   /note="Domain:cl01108:BrnT_toxin Ribonuclease toxin, BrnT,
FT                   of type II toxin-antitoxin system. BrnT is a ribonuclease
FT                   toxin of a type II toxin-antitoxin system that exhibits a
FT                   RelE-like fold. The antitoxin that neutralizes this toxin
FT                   is pfam14384. BrnT is found in bacteria, archaea,
FT                   bacteriophage, and plasmids. BrnT-BrnA forms a 2:2
FT                   tetrameric complex and autoregulates its own expression,
FT                   which is induced by a number of different environmental
FT                   stresses. Expression of BrnT alone results in cessation of
FT                   bacterial growth which can be rescued after subsequent
FT                   expression of BrnA. [Superfamily, Aligned:5-95,
FT                   Eval:5.9e-29, score:97.1]"
