FT                   /note="Domain:cl00360:5-FTHF_cyc-lig
FT                   5-formyltetrahydrofolate cyclo-ligase family. This enzyme,
FT                   5,10-methenyltetrahydrofolate synthetase, is also called
FT                   5-formyltetrahydrofolate cycloligase. Function of bacterial
FT                   proteins in this family was inferred originally from the
FT                   known activity of eukaryotic homologs. Recently, activity
FT                   was shown explicitly for the member from Mycoplasma
FT                   pneumonia. Members of this family from alpha- and
FT                   gamma-proteobacteria, designated ygfA, are often found in
FT                   an operon with 6S structural RNA, and show a similar
FT                   pattern of high expression during stationary phase. The
FT                   function may be to deplete folate to slow 1-carbon
